<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Bayer unit workers continue strike.</title>
<headline>Belgian Bayer unit workers continue strike.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at Agfa-Gevaert NV, the Belgian photographic products unit of German chemicals group Bayer AG, said on Friday they would strike &quot;until the finish&quot; over stalled negotiations about a global deal with management.</p>
<p>&quot;(We'll strike) until everybody's back at the negotiating table and they are coming out again with (a deal),&quot; a socialist trade union spokesman told BRTN radio.</p>
<p>The workers went on strike on Thursday after talks to renew a collective workers agreement (CAO) broke down.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
